"41da8ad0-e0fc-5f39-8eb7-c4706c551e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-118976" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dcd36221e7ad293f0aac1ab99ece80641cb077efd05adc168a552e97d86100c8.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{AD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$ is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$ is true. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}.$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{FA}$ is false. Indeed, $\\overset{\\to }{AD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}\\ne \\overset{\\to }{FA}$ since they have the opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3aa84ae8-6663-5aa1-844b-89090bcce735" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048822 :topic/id #uuid "c2fc5214-795d-5bfe-b226-459801a3c888" :topic/math-academy-id 3276 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Directly Integrable Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e35797-c4cc-588f-a334-6e167d806dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448072} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6dc8e7-0a87-5da6-a74f-4c8397d0c042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf6dc8e7-0a87-5da6-a74f-4c8397d0c042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448073} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f75b47-16b6-5dd6-a760-d4992c5c2524" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=0,$ the slope field has a positive slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d765046-e075-5330-b681-0d916148575b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448074} {:answer/id #uuid "76d506ba-3407-5dfa-b117-bc384b0cc378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76d506ba-3407-5dfa-b117-bc384b0cc378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448075} :answer-field/id #uuid "9178f62a-187a-5cd8-94b0-3a0de5cf57e5" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77619b7f-1d91-56eb-b4d3-056373fa62fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448076} {:answer/id #uuid "817742eb-aa8e-5d46-ab84-dc12f41876a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77619b7f-1d91-56eb-b4d3-056373fa62fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448076} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac315583-34df-5bdd-a20d-a5eaf525c2fe" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=-2,$ the slope field has a positive slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19539888-a72b-5a8c-9bb4-399cabb49fb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119194" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=0,$ the slope field has a positive slope” is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}=2(0)+2=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is positive for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is equal to $2$ for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal” is true. Consider a point of the form $(-1,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,y)}=2(-1)+2=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(-1,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=-2,$ the slope field has a positive slope” is false. Consider a point of the form $(-2,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,y)}=2(-2)+2=-2<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(-2,y)$ is negative for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(-2,y)$ is equal to $-2$ for any $y.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point along the line $x=0,$ the slope field has a positive slope”; “At every point along the line $x=-1,$ the slope field is horizontal” only.\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8d/8d40c405f3f4db66a18e06a5327e86600081a6bc57b502ebed9c94471a0d5857.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3aa84ae8-6663-5aa1-844b-89090bcce735" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048822 :topic/id #uuid "c2fc5214-795d-5bfe-b226-459801a3c888" :topic/math-academy-id 3276 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Directly Integrable Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b26889df-f672-5f76-93ae-d98cd0173db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448078} {:answer/id #uuid "9437deb6-cc24-5774-a85c-1c4a52d73000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9437deb6-cc24-5774-a85c-1c4a52d73000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448079} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ff68659-ffc5-5fed-89d6-2e1daf181229" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=2,$  the slope field has a negative slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b94d37f8-23ff-5f0d-9fe1-b5d1972b75ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448080} {:answer/id #uuid "f37c784e-dc31-553e-8974-bc26d2b13ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f37c784e-dc31-553e-8974-bc26d2b13ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448081} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ec99642-e984-5d80-aafb-a5b6a95e4ba8" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field is horizontal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d857a423-2edb-5832-8490-16d6fda1aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448082} {:answer/id #uuid "b4594e53-bf79-501e-9810-9917d4099c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d857a423-2edb-5832-8490-16d6fda1aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448082} :answer-field/id #uuid "71854520-8289-544a-af3f-146efa12ed30" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope of the slope field does not vary" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6eca5ac4-aebb-5558-a54f-a273db0d7d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119206" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}-3x$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=2,$  the slope field has a negative slope” is true. Consider a point of the form $(2,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,y)}={2}^{2}-3(2)=-2,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(2,y)$ is negative for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field is horizontal” is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}={0}^{2}-3(0)=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(0,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $y=1,$ the slope of the slope field does not vary” is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,1)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,1)}={x}^{2}-3x,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(x,1)$ depends on $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point along the line $x=2,$  the slope field has a negative slope”; “At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field is horizontal” only.\n\nWe can use the information given by the true statements to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e2/e2ce8d7df3d0ceee4f8c9dcf368940006f1266a751c2f8e5ea8afdcfb90bf7ac.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3aa84ae8-6663-5aa1-844b-89090bcce735" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048822 :topic/id #uuid "c2fc5214-795d-5bfe-b226-459801a3c888" :topic/math-academy-id 3276 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Directly Integrable Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2d8ae0-c0d6-5028-83c2-1907754129e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448084} {:answer/id #uuid "bf134717-da17-5a2a-9007-2d2221e992a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf134717-da17-5a2a-9007-2d2221e992a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448085} :answer-field/id #uuid "901b068f-d1cc-55f3-9847-0c9f43ba1c7f" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=1,$  the slope field is horizontal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "977772b0-6d10-5f44-acb1-e4ff1e286577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448086} {:answer/id #uuid "676ee669-c4da-5472-a261-dd93452e6756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "676ee669-c4da-5472-a261-dd93452e6756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448087} :answer-field/id #uuid "530e3e75-0636-5430-906f-95c911d5ecef" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field has a positive slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d2a31a5-7247-5293-a978-37ef33cf6ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448088} {:answer/id #uuid "35d8e55d-d1cf-56aa-9069-dba43421e95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35d8e55d-d1cf-56aa-9069-dba43421e95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448089} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb4c7df5-21a8-5c7b-809a-f0c5deea3353" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope of the slope field varies" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e9d7c3e-9e55-5477-a8a9-aed5b3e5371d" :question/math-academy-id "q-119209" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-{x}^{3}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $x,$ the slope does not vary with $y.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=1,$  the slope field is horizontal” is true. Consider a point of the form $(1,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,y)}=1-{1}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(1,y)$ is horizontal for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field has a positive slope” is true. Consider a point of the form $(0,y)$ where $y$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,y)}=1-{0}^{3}=1>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(0,y)$ is positive for any $y.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(0,y)$ is equal to $1$ for any $y.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope of the slope field varies” is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,2)}=1-{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope of the slope field at the point $(x,2)$ depends on $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point along the line $x=1,$  the slope field is horizontal”; “At every point along the line $x=0,$  the slope field has a positive slope”; “At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope of the slope field varies”.\n\nWe can use the information given by the true statements to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/85/85d8f71c4680a56d5722b87fa5f7b2a7623fd2457f540c2cd15cd3bfa29694f3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172036 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1343e4de-56ee-563c-bdc8-f8c0cdc54f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Slope Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048179 :topic/id #uuid "8633737d-b07f-5466-99f0-a422586920c4" :topic/math-academy-id 3351 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Autonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48fd0ccc-8019-5758-8e77-495fa768b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448090} {:answer/id #uuid "fe55d5cc-3414-57dc-afa9-1c945f72f958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48fd0ccc-8019-5758-8e77-495fa768b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448090} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f9bfa14-f07a-57a1-8e61-d35ecbdf56eb" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope field has a positive slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4f0280-3057-5fc5-bdf9-358fb92ea26c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448092} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebcc34f-d79b-5cfb-9967-eab231751295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ebcc34f-d79b-5cfb-9967-eab231751295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448093} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9960db6-909e-50a8-aea1-4eb176bb9f4b" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449086} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "def0803c-91ae-5f1c-867c-5a15b7bfeae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448094} {:answer/id #uuid "f09f6bdc-1380-5507-a746-f5a83382df19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "def0803c-91ae-5f1c-867c-5a15b7bfeae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448094} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec478c5-09f5-5db6-a6bd-44dce48ef43f" :answer-field/key "At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a negative slope" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95486801-04a3-50a0-ad5b-8d31467cc59e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119324" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThis is an autonomous equation because the right-hand side is a function of $y$ only. This means that, for a fixed value of $y,$ the slope does not vary with $x.$ \n\nNow, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $y=2,$ the slope field has a positive slope” is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,2)}=-2<0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,2)$ is negative for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,2)$ is equal to $-2$ for any $x.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal” is true. Consider a point of the form $(x,0)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,0)}=-0=0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,0)$ is horizontal for any $x.$\n\n- Statement “At every point along the line $y=-2,$ the slope field has a negative slope” is false. Consider a point of the form $(x,-2)$ where $x$ is arbitrary. We have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,-2)}=-(-2)=2>0,\n$$\n\nand this implies that the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is positive for any $x.$ Moreover, the slope at the point $(x,-2)$ is equal to $2$ for any $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point along the line $y=0,$ the slope field is horizontal” only.\n\nWe can use this information to begin sketching the slope field, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8f/8fc0b5be5c9147c29410ff7a082316403302f2bce7ec25c665ab7ccc5bf90b0f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "932fd48b-8935-57c7-8293-eb9a71377d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461869} {:answer/id #uuid "56de3e7c-351f-5781-a84d-24f381e2d6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56de3e7c-351f-5781-a84d-24f381e2d6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461870} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf424628-63d2-57e6-be5d-101e46f767e7" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a3ca570-83fb-5da6-a3be-00fe526ae7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461871} {:answer/id #uuid "d7703abf-77ac-5af8-a67c-13948de7e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7703abf-77ac-5af8-a67c-13948de7e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461872} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15d3225-3000-55f2-ab15-7cd57eec9d48" :answer-field/key "The point $(-5,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f70e53bd-3eda-5218-a9f5-043d667b741e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461873} {:answer/id #uuid "aed5fbc2-44e7-5a80-8887-c43bc5e676bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aed5fbc2-44e7-5a80-8887-c43bc5e676bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461874} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d3e201f-dd08-57df-b785-f1e323a09839" :answer-field/key "The point $(5,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3510664b-2f53-5d5d-9a15-f28784a8e0c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11961" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,-3),(0,5),(2,-5).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,-2),(-5,0),(5,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(3,-2)$”; “The point $(-5,0)$”; “The point $(5,2)$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092346 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2371a64-5e91-5caa-91c0-f6c7ff572c70" :knowledge-point/title "Rotating an Object About the Origin" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049891 :topic/id #uuid "1bf5a1e3-35e9-581e-b44a-fa6e4c7b4bff" :topic/math-academy-id 932 :topic/title "Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d2902e-fe58-53b7-9bea-3127e6359fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461875} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac292f-81f0-5439-8f10-2af989375112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac292f-81f0-5439-8f10-2af989375112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461876} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb618ec-27a1-5c30-9f69-da8678e0d24e" :answer-field/key "The point $(0,\\sqrt{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a721534-6ddd-57ca-b5b5-8ac253bdf5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461877} {:answer/id #uuid "022bbf55-1062-54d5-aec8-1dd458f8a82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a721534-6ddd-57ca-b5b5-8ac253bdf5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461877} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c8256e-8dfb-5fb9-b88c-844f3965001a" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e47ca5-94e2-5e80-99e4-0cf645a6be09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461879} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff35a1a-1e27-5a4c-99ed-19f6834bf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e47ca5-94e2-5e80-99e4-0cf645a6be09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461879} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6b0bfd-1f1e-5700-8876-61f888ab4569" :answer-field/key "The point $(-5,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34508741-6c7f-54ff-a124-34cef40dd55c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11967" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(-1,2),(2,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under a **clockwise** rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians about the origin?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\theta =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into the above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the transformation, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the rotation $R$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{ }\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are \n\n$$\n(0,\\sqrt{2}),\\,(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,(-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(0,\\sqrt{2})$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049891 :topic/id #uuid "1bf5a1e3-35e9-581e-b44a-fa6e4c7b4bff" :topic/math-academy-id 932 :topic/title "Rotations as Linear Transformations"} :activity/title "Rotations as Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557868} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558598}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049213 :topic/id #uuid "e3ec8239-fcb5-5753-aa06-6c1a1dcb3ccb" :topic/math-academy-id 988 :topic/title "Inverting Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f05073e6-bfb4-5b8d-8db4-310e7dfa5a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} {:answer/id #uuid "f8cc566f-6c98-5ea4-b7be-dc39ac81a01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f05073e6-bfb4-5b8d-8db4-310e7dfa5a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461881} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5f69b8e-f7c4-5e0a-9f1d-00394a46cc6a" :answer-field/key "The point $(2,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04970681-2afb-550f-9388-bd0cba68f0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} {:answer/id #uuid "2edff474-152a-55c0-91ad-ecc28535f220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04970681-2afb-550f-9388-bd0cba68f0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461883} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa044452-e56e-5ba8-a718-24f5a020ad8c" :answer-field/key "The point $(0,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5254f4e8-74dd-5cce-a282-1148360c51fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461885} {:answer/id #uuid "f5978d27-0a47-584a-877f-15e8629c4892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5978d27-0a47-584a-877f-15e8629c4892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461886} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdc29db2-90c6-5990-862a-26c63df63336" :answer-field/key "The point $(-5,-8)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d13de60-db83-5fa3-ae76-e5805b3d5848" :question/math-academy-id "q-11974" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,-2),(-3,2),(2,2),$ and $(-1,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-(-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(0,-2),(-5,-8),(0,2),(0,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The point $(-5,-8)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048489 :topic/id #uuid "a42b014b-839c-50bc-ab24-36abe7ee39ce" :topic/math-academy-id 3352 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de7b235-2d26-5638-9c0e-50fbf024a420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437558} {:answer/id #uuid "a52d85f3-9510-5691-8cd4-aec1cbec2217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52d85f3-9510-5691-8cd4-aec1cbec2217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437559} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3564637-e4ca-5adf-93e8-018d20d50745" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c57c046d-8a73-5f59-9a49-b2aed7a95848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437560} {:answer/id #uuid "70926e08-7c1e-54d5-abf7-3b2825ba6a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70926e08-7c1e-54d5-abf7-3b2825ba6a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437561} :answer-field/id #uuid "569f6144-ac61-57e2-9faa-b2202fc52224" :answer-field/key "At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81024236-c12a-5269-b2cd-e687e5de0a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437562} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9cd6b7-f2cf-568e-a96b-b42a586b87cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d9cd6b7-f2cf-568e-a96b-b42a586b87cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437563} :answer-field/id #uuid "e68102cc-579c-585f-8f10-9a83a65a0a06" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d92f1990-38b8-544d-a68e-c6daa48b1c4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119766" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive”; “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048489 :topic/id #uuid "a42b014b-839c-50bc-ab24-36abe7ee39ce" :topic/math-academy-id 3352 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf9f9a0-fe1d-58a6-a9a8-b5a5e2a9514b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437564} {:answer/id #uuid "c6011e7b-933f-5512-8d31-3053e17fd0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf9f9a0-fe1d-58a6-a9a8-b5a5e2a9514b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecff95c2-727a-5dae-ab02-1414391132f2" :answer-field/key "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791f7229-c5a9-5faf-8875-969a85713e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437566} {:answer/id #uuid "a8d04d15-d334-5842-ab9f-31f5f6d0fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "791f7229-c5a9-5faf-8875-969a85713e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437566} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdf80c4-0c0f-5731-bd95-650894071c56" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f793cf-e920-5057-905e-6cd6b37d67be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437568} {:answer/id #uuid "42e66d50-d188-5d08-9d22-fe5a8a4b8fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42e66d50-d188-5d08-9d22-fe5a8a4b8fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437569} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f69ac8-557d-5583-a34f-bae77d1add4a" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e15411d6-1039-50b8-8bc5-cef852747aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-119769" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-5xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-5xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048489 :topic/id #uuid "a42b014b-839c-50bc-ab24-36abe7ee39ce" :topic/math-academy-id 3352 :topic/title "Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2acc8d45-b3cb-5472-808a-0ded96068ea4"