:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc49fe00-4ce7-5ef1-a571-3c5c05755fd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-1212" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N∣-1\\le x+1\\le 3}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣{x}^{2}\\le -2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $-1\\le x+1\\le 3,$ that is to say, $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={1,2}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}\\le -2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB=∅.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $0\\in A$ but $0\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. The empty set is a subset of every set.\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A⊈B$; $B⊆A$; $A⊇B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f6a5209-1dd7-5528-9bd5-5bc7fb3d7b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462019} {:answer/id #uuid "e85d203a-19e9-56f3-ac3a-c0e656286c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85d203a-19e9-56f3-ac3a-c0e656286c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462020} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6db83a-49a3-58ae-bedd-1966d3e3fe74" :answer-field/key "The point $(-3,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e74dce9-fc12-5890-b1ba-090c92c360ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462021} {:answer/id #uuid "934072a1-cc59-57ad-b108-ba577635684a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e74dce9-fc12-5890-b1ba-090c92c360ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462021} :answer-field/id #uuid "db271adc-484d-5ee6-9806-c7fd21b54d00" :answer-field/key "The point $(-3,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6228b74-5ee9-5e84-aff0-9ab707e83eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462023} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdb6908-c816-5640-9e06-d159c59a48ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cdb6908-c816-5640-9e06-d159c59a48ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462024} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd923679-cb67-593b-8dca-a5d88dd55567" :answer-field/key "The point $(1,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e3e3b1c-0354-523c-88ee-c0560a031e2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-12124" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(-2,-1),(1,3),(2,-3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${90}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(1,-2),(-3,1),(3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(-3,1)$”; “The point $(1,-2)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048712 :topic/id #uuid "b784cbd9-6f0d-5689-9a0e-6e19dfca34c7" :topic/math-academy-id 931 :topic/title "Right-Angle Rotations as Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7