representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=2$ is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-2)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $det(A)=2$; “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049035 :topic/id #uuid "d53c1458-9af5-589b-8d7b-d3dbe4e7a946" :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b72bc2-de18-5a31-bfdf-fdac912549a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448164} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e96f5b-82de-5376-876d-7a84ae9bf74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3e96f5b-82de-5376-876d-7a84ae9bf74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448165} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e27ccb4-b5c0-5a9a-8d03-5e3c15a85d08" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25dc899-6e5e-5d48-a151-181957ec1b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448166} {:answer/id #uuid "89240879-1b78-5c81-9622-9647e99c0713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89240879-1b78-5c81-9622-9647e99c0713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448167} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5172e33-9775-5938-831d-f44ab65c3dcd" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7080029-1010-516b-b69b-6dabb70fcd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448168} {:answer/id #uuid "d634558c-1872-5b5c-9aff-88f13ebecb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7080029-1010-516b-b69b-6dabb70fcd57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448168} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe4987e-3c97-588e-81f0-536e77edb94f" :answer-field/key "The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e2308b7-d41e-52ef-9ac3-a8e7e1231e38" :question/math-academy-id "q-124326" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-1$ is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$; $det(A)=-1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049035 :topic/id #uuid "d53c1458-9af5-589b-8d7b-d3dbe4e7a946" :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f764cc6-1478-5e54-bd9c-3364a17fabe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17