that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2v+1 \\\\ 4u-v-5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-4$ is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix}=0\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-2)=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050189 :topic/id #uuid "34f05255-901a-5db2-9431-e0175ef37691" :topic/math-academy-id 3357 :topic/title "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecde6e98-53fd-5ddd-bdc1-6ff205d00d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462139} {:answer/id #uuid "f49d1e0e-f360-53d6-9140-755bc53425ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f49d1e0e-f360-53d6-9140-755bc53425ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462140} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82752cf-bf54-5079-8c9f-a8fa8464cd75" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17fa137d-526a-57e9-8c8d-806b8a6e7139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462141} {:answer/id #uuid "482d1113-1761-5039-8696-fb7a9c674eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17fa137d-526a-57e9-8c8d-806b8a6e7139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462141} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c5e294-13bc-5717-9f9c-3fef7f5d4399" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6953b99-2176-55bb-9f0e-69ab32d7d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462143} {:answer/id #uuid "b13b7134-2fe3-59e1-90c8-cc035011e284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6953b99-2176-55bb-9f0e-69ab32d7d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df54704-5657-56ec-913b-dbeb0cf13cfe" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+x\\ne 0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "387d1688-e72e-5fdc-bd02-55d9c19c099b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124775" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$ is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge x.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}$ is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole (containing all points of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1$).\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+x\\ne 0}$ is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=-x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050189 :topic/id #uuid "34f05255-901a-5db2-9431-e0175ef37691" :topic/math-academy-id 3357 :topic/title "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18243450-8bc5-5ba5-92ae-2a12b967b1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462145} {:answer/id #uuid "53526394-7618-5253-b8b8-39da508afb42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18243450-8bc5-5ba5-92ae-2a12b967b1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462145} :answer-field/id #uuid "701895d0-d3f5-5fd1-99cc-2ef0e7db9adb" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462826} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb1353f6-b0c0-5194-a209-45cfa89e9762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462147} {:answer/id #uuid "67103826-f812-5a9c-a5d1-e93ca05c2123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67103826-f812-5a9c-a5d1-e93ca05c2123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462148} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24c9f12-a9c4-502d-a521-d96ff0a52d43" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "973fe3d8-28f4-5ce5-afa3-e107736244b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462149} {:answer/id #uuid "2f92d4a6-c6ba-5890-bc7a-b9c3b83bf58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "973fe3d8-28f4-5ce5-afa3-e107736244b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462149} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b065414-05f8-5b5f-b809-0e2f2975f5ea" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd4c2e21-ea3a-5149-9740-8c2a599beff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124782" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$ is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$  is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$ is *not* simply connected.  The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the coordinate axes.  Thus, the region is formed by four disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050868 :topic/id #uuid "6cc04ddb-ad7b-51e8-8f9d-c71c72f8e9d4" :topic/math-academy-id 684 :topic/title "Convergence of Geometric Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2b34516-3ea8-584f-906e-e8611ac12828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462151} {:answer/id #uuid "291a43ca-613d-5a0d-9ab8-0303748e2957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2b34516-3ea8-584f-906e-e8611ac12828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462151} :answer-field/id #uuid "c25edcf3-d687-539e-bcd5-23dfed8b3afb" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }0.25{(1.1)}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f07d465a-cb07-59a2-ba0c-6485c2e2203c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462153} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb4f3ab-0ab6-5c87-9b0a-255c44be23cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f07d465a-cb07-59a2-ba0c-6485c2e2203c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462153} :answer-field/id #uuid "90d4580d-2f8a-562a-9bab-ac4b9c80c2c2" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4}{(-\\frac{5}{2})}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ee1f91-30b1-5897-9518-97a3b6a06b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462155} {:answer/id #uuid "9f36d431-b912-544f-a3f7-12ba6a12bb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ee1f91-30b1-5897-9518-97a3b6a06b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462155} :answer-field/id #uuid "6645ce3c-ff42-5463-89e7-d2920082b362" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }\\frac{{3}^{n-1}}{{2}^{n}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ce3cd55-5416-540d-b4b8-b6e9967829be" :question/math-academy-id "q-124906" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }0.25{(1.1)}^{n}$ starts with $n=0.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{{a}_{0}} & =\\frac{0.25{(1.1)}^{1}}{0.25{(1.1)}^{0}} \\\\  & =1.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4}{(-\\frac{5}{2})}^{n}$ starts with $n=1.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}{(-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}{\\frac{1}{4}{(-\\frac{5}{2})}^{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }\\frac{{3}^{n-1}}{{2}^{n}}$ starts with $n=2.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}} & =\\frac{(\\frac{{3}^{3-1}}{{2}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{3}^{2-1}}{{2}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{3}})}{(\\frac{3}{{2}^{2}})} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{3}})(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050868 :topic/id #uuid "6cc04ddb-ad7b-51e8-8f9d-c71c72f8e9d4" :topic/math-academy-id 684 :topic/title "Convergence of Geometric Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fad3c269-bef4-5865-aab8-6a0b35ec71d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462157} {:answer/id #uuid "98f93dc7-fe53-5026-b0cd-64e62c2fe4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f93dc7-fe53-5026-b0cd-64e62c2fe4da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462158} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4bcc406-44ad-54a6-861c-b4d287a6c9c5" :answer-field/key "$162+108+72+48+⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41ce7a7b-500a-5304-8f49-f2cb53102966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462159} {:answer/id #uuid "835a9efd-c099-5f5a-bcff-920b942ffed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "835a9efd-c099-5f5a-bcff-920b942ffed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462160} :answer-field/id #uuid "967ad5b0-4dd2-5a4e-bc8d-8387b1e60467" :answer-field/key "$1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "851361d5-17fd-547e-b912-e443e6fd861f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462161} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb42a01-ec53-52aa-b27b-17d3dc70d8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cb42a01-ec53-52aa-b27b-17d3dc70d8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462162} :answer-field/id #uuid "a76e67d3-a0bb-584a-9e18-bb2f2fd0f103" :answer-field/key "$-10-9-8.1-7.29-⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "893c9c3b-88dc-5138-95d4-8126574b5268" :question/math-academy-id "q-124913" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $162+108+72+48+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{108}{162} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{4})}{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $-10-9-8.1-7.29-⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{-9}{-10} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, series $162+108+72+48+⋯$, $1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+⋯$, and $-10-9-8.1-7.29-⋯$ converge."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Discrete Random Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048368 :topic/id #uuid "99cc78ff-5612-5e6a-a347-8c2389044b69" :topic/math-academy-id 1290 :topic/title "Probability Mass Functions of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afd9a568-8c3a-5db1-9df7-bea0a134ca5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462163} {:answer/id #uuid "4761d927-b65a-5fe8-9e03-e8d4fbed528e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd9a568-8c3a-5db1-9df7-bea0a134ca5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462163} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c25aa8a-c2d5-5b3a-8ee2-4c94e88ab1cc" :answer-field/key "The time it takes for a student to complete math homework" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3681eeac-9e8f-559d-951e-a7e413b1c642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462165} {:answer/id #uuid "a1349f94-fafc-5f1b-8ea5-98e220143f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1349f94-fafc-5f1b-8ea5-98e220143f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462166} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c3754d-055a-54bb-9366-8ad968917b20" :answer-field/key "The number of hours you spend jogging in a week" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "852602ce-afd8-5ba8-a935-74f8a3c60eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462167} {:answer/id #uuid "a6305496-817c-5b29-a238-07677383adce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6305496-817c-5b29-a238-07677383adce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462168} :answer-field/id #uuid "62efaa6d-07eb-57d3-b082-03ee657e3223" :answer-field/key "The number of candies in a jar" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35c884a2-41d0-58e7-ba4f-0c197a382264" :question/math-academy-id "q-125075" :question/problem "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The time it takes for a student to complete math homework” does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\n- Statement “The number of hours you spend jogging in a week” describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and it has finitely many possible values: $0,1,2,3,…$\n\n- Statement “The number of candies in a jar” describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and it has finitely many possible values: $0,1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of hours you spend jogging in a week”; “The number of candies in a jar” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048434 :topic/id #uuid "9ef976b2-cf49-59ec-9689-0ec6f4a92d3c" :topic/math-academy-id 288 :topic/title "The Mean Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417b034a-4a1b-57ea-ae71-c3692dd9c074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462169} {:answer/id #uuid "366f4957-2ec0-53a1-aaec-db78bf39c189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "366f4957-2ec0-53a1-aaec-db78bf39c189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462170} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33e6574-4ffa-5b8b-8bd3-5160e7158367" :answer-field/key "$f(x)={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2848015f-fd1c-524b-9770-6641ede3f19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462171} {:answer/id #uuid "505d7bac-6415-5832-a400-b6da7b039903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2848015f-fd1c-524b-9770-6641ede3f19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462171} :answer-field/id #uuid "9753bc53-75e5-5715-a073-5b1b466537bd" :answer-field/key "$g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee75ead-b5ed-510b-a4c5-d9a5d1757af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462173} {:answer/id #uuid "7796dc8d-ca52-55f7-aa70-af05b82e9eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7796dc8d-ca52-55f7-aa70-af05b82e9eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462174} :answer-field/id #uuid "629cf843-1a02-5f46-991b-cdafd055537c" :answer-field/key "$h(x)=x|x|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79dcb2e6-ddac-560d-acd7-0aceed9cb202" :question/math-academy-id "q-125259" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1]?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1],$ the function must be continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$ is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=x|x|$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions $f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=x|x|$ satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6f84f1-683f-5d00-9604-34d4790cb9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb212b19-0efe-5595-8a6e-e47cc9adaa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a39db3-475c-5e0a-801d-11e7e55a57ab" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe3f7d-d217-5537-9b72-5552de904647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462177} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6588a-1243-5256-a273-81f127138027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462178} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8dffca-0ed9-5da1-995f-1364b3fbea05" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea2a08c-0d10-592a-9aa9-d6c47c1f74d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32ca2cc7-24f7-507a-9285-aa88fa019e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462179} :answer-field/id #uuid "68723449-ccac-55e8-b16a-59ae779fc661" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4fa44014-b4ce-590d-a5cb-5c0b5e464aaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-125392" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dca985dc352c45477dbb6ada86ad5a9cfa4404969510191a1955e59b082709fe.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false, while statement ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves around $C,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/eb/eb4da8143700c7d31e0ceacd09ac76a8d1bcb10379a34dce5b59d48f2ae58c13.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ remains unchanged.\n\n![](images/70/70a473397216589350f63482ab3e36cb1247e7825046c70642254c8514564b00.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a312728-759b-5a18-bc9a-7a468e2c468e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} {:answer/id #uuid "b006ccd8-dbf9-52a5-8de6-8656396b4437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a312728-759b-5a18-bc9a-7a468e2c468e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462181} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09c4b26-8176-500e-9d72-7fa8141a088c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822889f3-1878-5472-943f-bc21421aa019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462183} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cd909-af16-5666-9ee5-08e066d042c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cd909-af16-5666-9ee5-08e066d042c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462184} :answer-field/id #uuid "e45bb2d9-7504-598f-8971-17193667fabf" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c27fd31-ee21-5aab-a03c-e98f38a45ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462185} {:answer/id #uuid "e661237d-bcf6-5e01-b2dc-8992ab58d984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e661237d-bcf6-5e01-b2dc-8992ab58d984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462186} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebc3f15f-2730-55a5-bdbe-6cc6317a24d4" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a58b62d-04d0-5a47-b1b2-408fc180c352" :question/math-academy-id "q-125487" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9da7dc42ad4e9eb5b6df7c42f06d7a0f7767820693f8e99e073c7b8bd7e93441.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/14/14e94a2c5d0faabff1beeadeccb6999aa2edd71fce06fff8a2655db74e585eba.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/c5/c54487081f2150216b7e41b1351f0f7b19c794b140297789f19d9afe830bd7b1.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$; ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "I