tement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/05/059731f0cac61f19382172192c6a9f7f366ecb758767797f9bc8311faa3865af.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$; ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "534628ec-e086-5d85-8e31-fc04c99a5f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462193} {:answer/id #uuid "aa45667f-b444-5719-9295-4e64b477febd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa45667f-b444-5719-9295-4e64b477febd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462194} :answer-field/id #uuid "046a9634-5223-5c56-bcba-e814a194fb0c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac9a279-64d9-5123-a34a-eb6c0ad0dfe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462195} {:ans