rem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-1,1]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-1,1].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,3]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=2.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-1,1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be60b44c-dc29-579a-8bbe-99cfeff6e423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463712} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed92d1a-34d6-595b-af27-4fada8783f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be60b44c-dc29-579a-8bbe-99cfeff6e423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463712} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbef85e1-8603-52aa-9d45-4ffbf68f775d" :answer-field/key "$(-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26443755-6945-5b03-a47f-d125aad2bcb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463714} {:answer/id #uuid "0a89f0d1-2951-5342-a42c-a0abf8cde927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true