 closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,4)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-2,4]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048980 :topic/id #uuid "d0f342d9-c70c-537f-9e04-f3b0beaf9c01" :topic/math-academy-id 2083 :topic/title "Row Echelon Form"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef8db13b-e915-5420-94d4-8b4458ce5fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463718} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7f11f5-58ab-59d2-afc1-9c23b39fc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7f11f5-58ab-59d2-afc1-9c23b39fc74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463719} :answer-field/id #uuid "d532a3a2-1d0e-50d0-a136-32281edc25ac" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb2d01b-af70-50a9-9015-bca80a3bb873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463720} {:answer/id #uuid "fee3e179-7eb5-50b9-a709-ed3f6c7925e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb2d01b-af70-50a9-9015-bca80a3bb873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463720} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac308526-bd74-527a-983e-81d7d32b6a13" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b761fd65-74b7-5657-9e3a-6bbb43c2ed38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463722} {:answer/id #uuid "046ac24b-d350-5155-929b-2bd3b846971a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b761fd65-74b7-5657-9e3a-6bbb43c2ed38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463722} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9104781-91ea-51e4-a150-d0602d23cb25" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e494fc8-9bc5-580b-afe6-c6a2f464663f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129220" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a46fb56-644a-52f0-b313-5e7bb7296c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463724} {:answer/id #uuid "79364f0e-086b-52ea-a70c-98b26093b5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a46fb56-644a-52f0-b313-5e7bb7296c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463724} :answer-field/id #uuid "bea28426-10d7-5367-be49-f9c216ba0970" :answer-field/key "$[0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464796} {:answer-field/choices [{: